# Figures an `@example` block writes when a page is run OUTSIDE the Documenter
# build -- extracted to a script for debugging, say. Documenter itself writes
# them into its build directory, so a copy at the repository root is always a
# measurement artifact and never a deliverable. Six of them reached a commit
# once; this is so it cannot happen twice.
# Figures written by the executed documentation blocks. `savefig` writes into
# the CWD, which is the repository root or `docs/` depending on where the build
# was launched from, so both are covered. The assets committed on purpose are
# the exception.
/*.svg
docs/*.svg
!docs/src/assets/*.svg

# Written by xgems wherever it is imported; the oracle bench in
# test/reference/ runs from the repository root.
xGEMS.log
